data a_secret_iam_policy_is_decided_by_two_models: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_secret_iam_policy_is_decided_by_two_models" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "two models each decide the expected IAM policy of the same secret: a second model binds cells for a resource another model already owns, each from its own hand-authored data. The writers are additive -- each adds its own cells and removes only its own -- so no single write is wrong, yet the pair produces a ping-pong: an external or earlier write of one model's bytes makes the other model's next plan see a diff, re-add cells, and churn the live policy. Every individual apply is green; the drift is only visible in the plan-phase setIamPolicy count, which no readback of the after-state reports. The green readback proves after-state equals model; it does NOT prove the calls were no-ops.",

    "SIGHTING, gunb-ai/gunbc gcp_iam_converge run 43880588775 (2026-11-16): the converge apply at 14:34Z issued setIamPolicy on six secrets whose live policy did not match its model -- printer-01-lan-access-code, printer-02-lan-access-code, tracker-web-stage-oauth-client-secret, mtcollins1-ssh-host-key, boot-medium-reader-ssh-key and bmc-srv15-admin -- fourteen minutes after the same day's bootstrap apply (14:20Z) had itself written bmc-srv15-admin's custody cells from its hand-authored custody arm. The printer/mtcollins1/boot-medium cells were present at 11-15 16:55 and absent before this run: something outside both models removed them, and converge re-added what its own model still declared. The manager ruled converge the single owner; the bootstrap's custody arm now DERIVES its bindings from the converge model's declared cells (gunbc.auth.gcp_iam_converge secret_custody_cells), and test.claim.gcp_iam_bootstrap_all_keys_witness holds the derivation with a claim per side, RED-verified by mutating the bootstrap side to a hand-authored different set.",

    "RUNG: mitigatable -- the witness claims refuse a second, different authoring over the custody population, but only after the population is listed in the witness universe. ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: a model that wants to bind cells for a secret takes them from the owning model's typed declaration -- the free construction of an IAM binding cell for a rostered secret outside the owner module is refused, so a second expected set cannot be written down anywhere.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
